d-56d9-bd28-ab237fb3be15" :question/math-academy-id "q-47449" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Find the slope of the normal line to the curve $y={x}^{2}+x$ at the point $(1,2).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)={x}^{2}+x.$ First, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+x) \\\\  & =2x+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the slope of the tangent at the point $(1,2):$\n\n$$\nm={f}^{′}(1)=2(1)+1=3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the normal line ${m}^{′}$ is\n\n$$\n{m}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-47449/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4a05f6c0-98ab-5197-922e-8e8dff1d4302"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-47449"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-103532/selection/852df530a82e413447a8b733db5e62e6c70e6d0be8b2e885cd815d17a6fb4ba1" :answer/id #uuid "8aa7f4ee-559f-584e-9a21-c244d64f3be2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103532/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "bdfde0b1-c906-5337-a0df-0c668a082fbe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103532/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "f8fbef3f-830a-5b02-8671-4ce91a4ecca6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103532/selection/25666b67a56594dd5245ec05e89d883db07d04362ab51dbc90c39ad20f7f9142" :answer/id #uuid "4b1dc0a6-b157-5ec3-9a98-2f62414ed8fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103532/selection/d3a7133ef1a1f6526aaec763d522f5ae075d8386a4606de90dcb93094f1d21d6" :answer/id #uuid "cd8cbafe-c47f-531b-9892-cd90a1e83ee6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "