of the normal line to the curve $y={x}^{2}-5$ at the point $(2,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)={x}^{2}-5.$ First, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}-5)=2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the slope of the tangent at the point $(2,-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={f}^{′}(2)=2(2)=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the normal line ${m}^{′}$ is\n\n$$\n{m}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-71524/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4a05f6c0-98ab-5197-922e-8e8dff1d4302"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71524"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-103531/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "8dd7f921-42e4-5cf8-9ba1-e20b085904db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103531/selection/2aef90071200a7bc65baa2d03f49803233ca7b2dc16865265136281ee914878b" :answer/id #uuid "7d8e7f13-0128-5f62-8243-068e418dc0fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103531/selection/35f5572ccca3a8c38d3ca06e2a92b51065f48e45d29833e19f4eb153cae096fc" :answer/id #uuid "d4859282-70e0-552b-8828-e43fcc39022e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103531/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" :answer/id #uuid "0d5d904e-1610-5676-a787-b4cb2f9a64cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103531/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "4aee79a0-82f0-5a57-9fd9-50245c95cb14" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103531/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "435d08fe-81af-56cb-a2e7-b26b52c4ed70" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-103531/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-103531/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-103531/selection/2aef90071200a7bc65baa2d03f49803233ca7b2dc16865265136281ee914878b" "q-103531/selection/35f5572ccca3a8c38d3ca06e2a92b51065f48e45d29833e19f4eb153cae096fc" "q-103531/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" "q-103531/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-103531" :question/id #uuid "0a59feec-a5b0-5815-a6e4-8461a44411c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-103531" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Find the slope of the normal line to the curve $y=2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}-2{x}^{2}$ at the point $(1,0).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}-2{x}^{2}.$ Computing the derivative ${f}^{′}(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}-2{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{3/2}-2{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =3{x}^{1/2}-4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute ${f}^{′}(1)$, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(1)=3(1)^{1/2}-4(1)=-1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the normal line ${m}^{′}$ is\n\n$$\n{m}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{m}=1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-103531/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4a05f6c0-98ab-5197-922e-8e8dff1d4302"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-103531"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-103543/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "827b0b85-5010-5ec0-9df5-40aa969e0cc0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate