(x)=\\frac{2}{{x}^{5}}+7x.$ Computing the derivative ${f}^{′}(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{2}{{x}^{5}}+7x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{-5}+7x) \\\\  & =-10{x}^{-6}+7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute ${f}^{′}(1)$, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(1)=-10(1)^{-6}+7=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the normal line ${m}^{′}$ is\n\n$$\n{m}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{m}=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-103543/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4a05f6c0-98ab-5197-922e-8e8dff1d4302"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-103543"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-342190/field-1/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer/id #uuid "71282172-bb03-581c-b587-7167173bb57d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342190/field-1/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "38c9d6ba-8068-5a75-88fb-0ce10dfaa9cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342190/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8ec52a40-e577-5cf1-9f3c-92667e03e3e9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-342190/field-1/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer-field/choices ["q-342190/field-1/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" "q-342190/field-1/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342190/field-2/12b7d840a997b0af25896f37c76d366155c72a970c1525c62ec119b69786f393" :answer/id #uuid "4a847893-ffea-5286-9e8c-81af2273cfa7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342190/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "44983d4e-a00f-5410-bf21-87280d8b73f7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-342190/field-2/12b7d840a997b0af25896f37c76d366155c72a970c1525c62ec119b69786f393" :answer-field/choices ["q-342190/field-2/12b7d840a997b0af25896f37c76d366155c72a970c1525c62ec119b69786f393"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342190" :question/id #uuid "d801a557-bb36-50c1-8317-3d5072ae1f0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-342190" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Find the equation of the normal line to the curve $y=\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt[3]{x}$ at the point $(\\frac{1}{8},\\frac{3}{4}).$\n\n$8x\\,+$\n{{field-1}}$\\cdot \\,y\\,=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt[3]{x}.$ First, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt[3]{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{1/3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{x}^{-2/3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the slope of the tangent at the point $(\\frac{1}{8},\\frac{3}{4}):$\n\n$$\nm={f}^{′}(\\frac{1}{8})=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt[3]{{(\\frac{1}{8})}^{2}}}=2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the normal line is\n\n$$\n{m}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-\\frac{3}{4} & =-\\frac{1}{2}(x-\\frac{1}{8}) \\\\ 16(y-\\frac{3}{4}) & =16\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})\\cdot (x-\\frac{1}{8}) \\\\ 16y-12 & =-8(x-\\frac{1}{8}) \\\\ 16y-12 & =-8x+1 \\\\ 8x+16\\cdot y & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-342190/field-1" "q-342190/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55a323ba-f2a7-5a49-abd4-a9812518ef8c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342190"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-342168/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "b84b4e3a-a5df-5496-9792-aa71771c5f81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342168/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "24355355-17a0-5ccb-8a06-77025f490d86" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-342168/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-342168/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342168/field-2/4644593a6ae896793c595e8a37cd468ba91be6a8038e715c4c88cddad1968793" :answer/id #uuid "96898260-8991-548c-a847-706338ff8c8a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342168/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "7d939833-5b0a-593c-bf25-f9df66d9a5e3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-342168/field-2/4644593a6ae896793c595e8a37cd468ba91be6a8038e715c4c88cddad1968793" :answer-field/choices ["q-342168/field-2/4644593a6ae896793c595e8a37cd468ba91be6a8038e715c4c88cddad1968793"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342168" :question/id #uuid "e7264db2-9dde-5fdd-9dff-7c1e888caf28" :question/math-academy-id "q-342168" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Find the equation of the normal line to the curve $y=\\frac{1}{8}{x}^{6}-\\frac{7}{4}{x}^{3}$ at the point $(2,-6).$\n\n$x\\,+$\n{{field-1}}$\\cdot \\,y\\,=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=\\frac{1}{8}{x}^{6}-\\frac{7}{4}{x}^{3}.$ First, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{8}{x}^{6}-\\frac{7}{4}{x}^{3})=\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{5}-\\frac{21}{4}{x}^{2}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the slope of the tangent at the point $(2,-6):$\n\n$$\nm={f}^{′}(2)=\\frac{3}{4}({2}^{5})-\\frac{21}{4}({2}^{2})=3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the normal line is\n\n$$\n{m}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(-6) & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (x-2) \\\\ -3(y+6) & =x-2 \\\\ -3y-18 & =x-2 \\\\ x+3\\cdot y & =-16.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-342168/field-1" "q-342168/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55a323ba-f2a7-5a49-abd4-a9812518ef8c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342168"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-47410/selection/0c91aee12841e83df8a63bea4f335135e4f592b0fef26da9fddc6b9cb7ae4e6d" :answer/id #uuid "08519b3a-97b6-5245-9ed9-75842ee68711" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "61" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47410/selection/78a7e48403bfc3aa596ef28683ea3912541da0aaa7377114be10358a6cb850d1" :answer/id #uuid "90ea3c86-7a25-529e-b33f-8888f0fe7f26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-81" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47410/selection/a5bcf5044d7131cdf0d721e80125a87ad3d00df1e947910bf38c9dd3889981de" :answer/id #uuid "51c29d6b-73b4-5613-9ef2-b1c56d654864" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "81" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47410/selection/07d13be2013e30923af5a143315b52581ff8ba40d0c80a016e8b9a5560d0140e" :answer/id #uuid "64452545-66ae-51c8-a67c-2a416bfb7390" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "71" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47410/selection/ed9233e3fc90a3fe2a01337d4aecb8be001489f8a46bc0efd8049c82d41ae4a0" :answer/id #uuid "4cdc2057-b94f-5b06-8234-175b6c3c8acb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-71" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47410/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "260aa085-bdb1-509e-a7c9-6c6f8bf8a9da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-47410/selection/a5bcf5044d7131cdf0d721e80125a87ad3d00df1e947910bf38c9dd3889981de" :answer-field/choices ["q-47410/selection/0c91aee12841e83df8a63bea4f335135e4f592b0fef26da9fddc6b9cb7ae4e6d" "q-47410/selection/78a7e48403bfc3aa596ef28683ea3912541da0aaa7377114be10358a6cb850d1" "q-47410/selection/a5bcf5044d7131cdf0d721e80125a87ad3d00df1e947910bf38c9dd3889981de" "q-47410/selection/07d13be2013e30923af5a143315b52581ff8ba40d0c80a016e8b9a5560d0140e" "q-47410/selection/ed9233e3fc90a3fe2a01337d4aecb8be001489f8a46bc0efd8049c82d41ae4a0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-47410" :question/id #uuid "414ee72f-747c-573a-9cad-a9cbdad6101a" :question/math-academy-id "q-47410" :question/is-example false :question/problem "The equation of the normal line to the curve $y=3{x}^{2}+4x$ at the point $(1,7)$ is given by $x+py=q$ where $p$ and $q$ are constants. Find the value of $p+q.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=3{x}^{2}+4x.$ First, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{2}+4x)=6x+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the slope of the tangent at the point $(1,7):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={f}^{′}(1)=6(1)+4=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the normal line ${m}^{′}$ is\n\n$$\n{m}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{10}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(7) & =-\\frac{1}{10}(x-1) \\\\ 10y-70 & =-x+1 \\\\ x+10y & =71.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p+q=10+71=81.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-47410/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55a323ba-f2a7-5a49-abd4-a9812518ef8c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-47410"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-47409/selection/801bcdd9cb6a10cec998162e05f71050c8aaf0c6974f095bdcaef715a09f4aee" :answer/id #uuid "3f513769-7378-5e17-b62b-1aa250e69edf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47409/selection/c59421689e9802bbe55dc885ef3b88a565922fc724e5a7225b403918fe48989b" :answer/id #uuid "1632a71f-b967-5bd3-8c73-eb9fe071d