\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}}-x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{x}^{-2}-x) \\\\  & =-8{x}^{-3}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the slope of the tangent at the point $(1,3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={f}^{′}(1)=-8(1)^{-3}-1=-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the normal line ${m}^{′}$ is\n\n$$\n{m}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{m}=\\frac{1}{9}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(3) & =\\frac{1}{9}(x-1) \\\\ 9y-27 & =x-1 \\\\ x-9y & =-26.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p-q=-9-(-26)=17.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-47409/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55a323ba-f2a7-5a49-abd4-a9812518ef8c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-47409"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-342162/field-1/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "b97c6a8a-e396-5c3c-9d0e-91d4f8962d57" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342162/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d929ed43-918c-51fe-82f0-6fa7fa13ddbe" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-342162/field-1/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer-field/choices ["q-342162/field-1/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342162/field-2/94b1e608a1bece13c117321c62644f2051416b0003719c2dd4b9ea44af9d6b64" :answer/id #uuid "cc7a2d36-09f8-5815-9bfb-b435098c4258" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-28" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342162/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "5da05495-4397-56ff-8ebc-6eef5a42d5b0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-342162/field-2/94b1e608a1bece13c117321c62644f2051416b0003719c2dd4b9ea44af9d6b64" :answer-field/choices ["q-342162/field-2/94b1e608a1bece13c117321c62644f2051416b0003719c2dd4b9ea44af9d6b64"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342162" :question/id #uuid "f1eef92d-2d17-5de7-8bd9-e36057891904" :question/math-academy-id "q-342162" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Find the equation of the normal line to the curve $y=6{x}^{2}-7x+4$ at the point $(0,4).$\n\n$x\\,-$\n{{field-1}}$\\cdot \\,y\\,=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=6{x}^{2}-7x+4.$ First, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6{x}^{2}-7x+4)=12x-7\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the slope of the tangent at the point $(0,4):$\n\n$$\nm={f}^{′}(0)=12(0)-7=-7\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the normal line is\n\n$$\n{m}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{m}=\\frac{1}{7}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-4 & =\\frac{1}{7}(x-0) \\\\ 7(y-4) & =x \\\\ 7y-28 & =x \\\\ x-7\\cdot y & =-28.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-342162/field-1" "q-342162/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55a323ba-f2a7-5a49-abd4-a9812518ef8c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342162"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-104073/selection/a8d21c191bb52f35e36b7998de659bcfd3f034bae56d7de9f7b5454525c340d2" :answer/id #uuid "ca569003-7200-53dc-becb-c5c0ef6958ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104073/selection/fe53418795c1f97ddd7606e407cb8eff6f4811e5807b92d77eabcf5c33e22d29" :answer/id #uuid "246671cb-963f-50f5-aafa-ae05eb3150cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,20)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104073/selection/c7d7f5865a04f287adfbc7ccac92458329d02c053e1fa27cc0df187ff8f49c48" :answer/id #uuid "cb40ced7-1bc1-5fd8-943b-3f837416c6a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,-4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104073/selection/434fbc6c10489094cc11d0f5fa0821781dae5725b81877eaf6ce63edda5844f4" :answer/id #uuid "dc92ea6c-546e-5c02-a31d-5db71be92a67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,-20)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104073/selection/66de7ff1b7cbf574d42b7bd40f9ad0ac12b5f01e0beb69f180f89bdfcac40c0b" :answer/id #uuid "08a71dde-9ffd-5cec-a32f-702f585847b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,-8)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104073/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "34d6edde-8082-5afb-b4b4-7f44dd8e85fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-104073/selection/fe53418795c1f97ddd7606e407cb8eff6f4811e5807b92d77eabcf5c33e22d29" :answer-field/choices ["q-104073/selection/a8d21c191bb52f35e36b7998de659bcfd3f034bae56d7de9f7b5454525c340d2" "q-104073/selection/fe53418795c1f97ddd7606e407cb8eff6f4811e5807b92d77eabcf5c33e22d29" "q-104073/selection/c7d7f5865a04f287adfbc7ccac92458329d02c053e1fa27cc0df187ff8f49c48" "q-104073/selection/434fbc6c10489094cc11d0f5fa0821781dae5725b81877eaf6ce63edda5844f4" "q-104073/selection/66de7ff1b7cbf574d42b7bd40f9ad0ac12b5f01e0beb69f180f89bdfcac40c0b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104073" :question/id #uuid "5f2145a2-4a3b-5f81-b58c-58ecc05ee736" :question/math-academy-id "q-104073" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Find where the normal line to the curve $f(x)=3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}$ at the point $(8,12)$ intersects the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{2/3}) \\\\  & =2{x}^{-1/3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\nm={f}^{′}(8)=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{8}}=1,\n$$\n\nand therefore the slope of the normal line is\n\n$$\n{m}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{m}=-1.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-12 & =-(x-8) \\\\ y & =-x+8+12 \\\\ y & =20-x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we find the point of intersection with the $y$-axis by setting $x=0$ and solving the resulting equation. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =20-0 \\\\ y & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the normal line intersects the $y$-axis at  $(0,20).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-104073/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ba61258-92a9-511e-891f-9e6adce2edb0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104073"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-342200/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer/id #uuid "db0cd71a-7e9b-5a54-b88a-373fc76fe3fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342200/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b01d0d0d-74d7-5993-9ebb-998c70c1883f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-342200/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer-field/choices ["q-342200/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342200/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "a5b1ba38-d11d-59bb-a8d6-46a5af09d418" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342200/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "f9462681-2595-5b9d-b3a5-3c3bd6ad79e0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-342200/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-342200/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342200" :question/id #uuid "d547e1c1-a0cb-5242-95b6-cf10768bcc9d" :question/math-academy-id "q-342200" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Find where the normal line to the curve $y=4-{x}^{2}$ at the point $(1,3)$ intersects the $x$-axis.\n\nThe normal line intersects the $x$-axis at\n$($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}} $).$" :question/worked-solution "Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4-{x}^{2})=-2x.\n$$\n\nSo the slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\nm={f}^{′}(1)=-2(1)=-2,\n$$\n\nand therefore the slope of the normal line is\n\n$$\n{m}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{(-2)}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-3 & =\\frac{1}{2}(x-1) \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{2}+3 \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we find the point of intersection with the $x$-axis by setting $y=0$ and solving the resulting equation. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{5}{2} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}x & =-\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ x & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the normal line intersects the $x$-axis at $(\\,-5,0\\,).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-342200/field-1" "q-342200/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ba61258-92a9-511e-891f-9e6adce2edb0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342200"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-342201/field-1/845beb42e162b04150b7b438e2c57c85fb9c5dc5bb6c7f2891f90687bf680708" :answer/id #uuid "586d4cf0-32d5-5f1f-b575-671f00d3e24e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342201/field-1/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" :answer/id #uuid "450d4247-2193-5884-bc24-36fc9af212a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342201/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "7b119a5a-7499-566f-8ad8-8fd4eb81017f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-342201/field-1/845beb42e162b04150b7b438e2c57c85fb9c5dc5bb6c7f2891f90687bf680708" :answer-field/choices ["q-342201/field-1/845beb42e162b04150b7b438e2c57c85fb9c5dc5bb6c7f2891f90687bf680708" "q-342201/field-1/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342201/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "883a065a-4ea0-5c8d-a890-a2aa7d8a164f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342201/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "7ac3d034-56e1-5503-8551-fc8dd1726b22" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-342201/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-342201/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342201" :question/id #uuid "871045b9-7122-52ce-88ea-7b0a5214a2f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-342201" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Find where the normal line to the curve $y=3{x}^{2}-6x+5$ at the point $(0,5)$ intersects the $x$-axis.\n\nThe normal line intersects the $x$-axis at\n$($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}} $).$" :question/worked-solution "Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{2}-6x+5)=6x-6.\n$$\n\nSo the slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\nm={f}^{′}(0)=6(0)-6=-6,\n$$\n\nand therefore the slope of the normal line is\n\n$$\n{m}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{(-6)}=\\frac{1}{6}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-5 & =\\frac{1}{6}(x-0) \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{6}x+5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we find the point of intersection with the $x$-axis by setting $y=0$ and solving the resulting equation. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{6}x+5 & =0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{6}x & =-5 \\\\ x & =-30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the normal line intersects the $x$-axis at $(\\,-30,0\\,).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-342201/field-1" "q-342201/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ba61258-92a9-511e-891f-9e6adce2edb0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342201"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-11124"] :question/worked-solution "Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{1/2}) \\\\  & ={x}^{-1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\nm={f}^{′}(1)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1}}=1,\n$$\n\nand therefore the slope of the normal line is\n\n$$\n{m}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{m}=-1.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-2 & =-1(x-1) \\\\ y & =-x+1+2 \\\\ y & =-x+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we find the point of intersection with the $y$-axis by setting $x=0$ and solving the resulting equation. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-0+3 \\\\ y & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the normal line intersects the $y$-axis at  $(0,3).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-104075/selection/981a2951e3fccc9ba81c501537ab818060069591c658c07fba6936fa5fd0dd27" :answer/id #uuid "65d2585c-2e1f-5c4d-b035-23d4271d7fbe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(3,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104075/selection/f2d3c1a7d39629bea356a024a828af9cb6c2c4f43d4ffe2776f9b7b220c6297b" :answer/id #uuid "94ef35e8-94e7-53c3-836b-7bf2ed2fa78a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(7,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104075/selection/ff992f3bfbf9256bb8a93ba4418b1d3fc4bf7775122685039de83403d09a1dca" :answer/id #uuid "54769853-ac06-5717-bda6-aab66c905c67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104075/selection/72d345d9b26260d53607453c165c4cc04463959dc5c36e19d717ec0f369232c4" :answer/id #uuid "8bd66a81-6297-5294-b79c-358bf0517640" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{1}{7},0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104075/selection/b770174d503061105b4b5143ffff874357af2108f0db047ca309ff6491c0d4be" :answer/id #uuid "2e9e61e3-3099-5473-8df7-019bdaca9185" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{1}{3},0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104075/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "90bd12a9-c2c6-5f43-b685-9095e24157fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-104075/selection/f2d3c1a7d39629bea356a024a828af9cb6c2c4f43d4ffe2776f9b7b220c6297b" :answer-field/choices ["q-104075/selection/981a2951e3fccc9ba81c501537ab818060069591c658c07fba6936fa5fd0dd27" "q-104075/selection/f2d3c1a7d39629bea356a024a828af9cb6c2c4f43d4ffe2776f9b7b220c6297b" "q-104075/selection/ff992f3bfbf9256bb8a93ba4418b1d3fc4bf7775122685039de83403d09a1dca" "q-104075/selection/72d345d9b26260d53607453c165c4cc04463959dc5c36e19d717ec0f369232c4" "q-104075/selection/b770174d503061105b4b5143ffff874357af2108f0db047ca309ff6491c0d4be"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104075" :question/id #uuid "d576f2ce-7e11-5d35-84cc-2026c401aedc" :question/math-academy-id "q-104075" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Find where the normal line to the curve $f(x)=2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}$ at the point $(1,2)$ intersects the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =3{x}^{1/2} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\nm={f}^{′}(1)=3\\sqrt{1}=3,\n$$\n\nand therefore the slope of the normal line is\n\n$$\n{m}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-2 & =-\\frac{1}{3}(x-1) \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{3}x+\\frac{1}{3}+2 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{3}x+\\frac{7}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we find the point of intersection with the $x$-axis by setting $y=0$ and solving the resulting equation. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{3}x+\\frac{7}{3} & =0 \\\\ x & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the normal line intersects the $x$-axis at  $(7,0).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-104075/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ba61258-92a9-511e-891f-9e6adce2edb0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104075"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
